        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "781f693f-2235-5dcd-b49d-3fc815a028e8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: The Periodic Table of Videos, Hello Internet\n- People: Brady Haran, Martyn Poliakoff, Peter Licence, Stephen Liddle, Debbie Kays, Neil Barnes, Sam Tang, CGP Grey\n- Organizations: University of Nottingham, BBC News, YouTube\n- Topics: chemical elements, the periodic table\n\nFacts:\n- Brady John Haran was born on 18 June 1976.\n- Brady Haran is an Australian-born British independent filmmaker and video journalist.\n- Brady Haran is known for educational videos and documentary films produced for BBC News.\n- Brady Haran is also known for his YouTube channels, especially Periodic Videos and Numberphile.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is a series of videos about chemical elements and the periodic table.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is published on YouTube.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is produced by Brady Haran.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos features Sir Martyn Poliakoff, Peter Licence, Stephen Liddle, Debbie Kays, Neil Barnes, Sam Tang, and others at the University of Nottingham.\n- Hello Internet is an audio podcast hosted by CGP Grey and Brady Haran.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f4746be6-87d0-5afb-80ac-1ef1dd9896ba",
        "text": "Page: The Periodic Table of Videos. Sentence: The Periodic Table of Videos is a series of videos about chemical elements and the periodic table.\nPage: The Periodic Table of Videos. Sentence: They are published on YouTube and produced by Brady Haran, a former BBC video journalist, featuring Sir Martyn Poliakoff (\"The Professor\"), Peter Licence, Stephen Liddle, Debbie Kays, Neil Barnes, Sam Tang and others at the University of Nottingham.\nPage: Brady Haran. Sentence: Brady John Haran ( , born 18 June 1976) is an Australian-born British independent filmmaker and video journalist who is known for his educational videos and documentary films produced for BBC News and also for his YouTube channels, the most notable being \"Periodic Videos\" and \"Numberphile\".\nPage: Hello Internet. Sentence: Hello Internet is an audio podcast hosted by YouTube content creators CGP Grey and Brady Haran.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
